.TH QFW-DEVICE-ACCESS.YAML 5 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw File Formats"
.SH NAME
qfw-device-access.yaml \- bind logical QFw devices to providers and credentials
.SH DESCRIPTION
The device-access configuration is a site-owned YAML file that maps logical
QFw device IDs to provider devices, API endpoints, and credential providers.
A service entry's
.B device-id
selects one device from this file.
.PP
The
.B service.device-access-config
field in
.BR qfw-site.yaml (5)
selects the active file. This separation allows a service manifest to describe
reusable QPM implementations while each site supplies its own devices,
endpoints, and credential integration.
.PP
Only the account running a device-backed QPM needs read access. The QPM manager
passes the selected path to the QPM process. Application processes do not
receive the file or provider credentials.
.SH QPUS MAPPING
The top-level
.B qpus
mapping contains one entry for each logical device ID.
.TP
.B provider
Provider implementation used by the device, such as
.BR iqm .
.TP
.B provider-device-id
Device name expected by the provider API. The logical QFw ID remains the key
under
.BR qpus .
.TP
.B url
Provider API endpoint.
.TP
.B credential-db
Path to a file-backed credential database. A relative path is resolved from
the directory containing the device-access file.
.TP
.B credential-provider
Name of an entry in the optional top-level
.B credential-providers
mapping. Use this instead of
.B credential-db
when a site integrates another credential source.
.TP
.B aliases
Optional alternate names that may resolve to this device.
.TP
.B resource-type
QRMI resource type to open for the device, such as
.B IQMServer
or
.BR IBMQiskitRuntimeService .
Optional when the provider serves only one resource type. An
.B ibm
device must set it, because IBM serves
.BR IBMQiskitRuntimeService ,
.BR IBMQuantumComputeService ,
and
.BR IBMQuantumSystem .
.TP
.B service-crn
IBM Cloud service instance CRN for an
.B ibm
device. QRMI requires one for every IBM resource type. An instance can serve
several devices and many users, and a user can be assigned to several
instances. This value is the default for users whose credential entry does not
name an instance, which a file credential database does with
.BR service_crn .
Quote the value, since a CRN ends in colons that YAML would otherwise misread.
.B QFW_IBM_SERVICE_CRN
overrides this default when set in the QPM's environment. A CRN in a
reservation's credential takes precedence over both.
.TP
.B iam-endpoint
IBM Cloud IAM endpoint that exchanges an API key for a token, for an
.B ibm
device. Optional. The default,
.BR https://iam.cloud.ibm.com ,
serves public IBM Cloud.
.B QFW_IBM_IAM_ENDPOINT
overrides it when set in the QPM's environment.
.SH CREDENTIAL PROVIDERS
The optional
.B credential-providers
mapping defines named credential integrations. Supported provider types include
.BR file ,
.BR no-secret ,
and Python plugin providers. A file provider uses
.B credential-db
or
.BR path .
Its optional fields include
.BR refresh-policy ,
.BR ttl-ns ,
and
.BR ttl-seconds .
A plugin provider uses
.B module
and may select a class with
.BR class .
.SH SECURITY
The device-access file contains device endpoints, credential-provider
references, and IBM service instance CRNs. A referenced file credential
database contains provider secrets
and must be readable only by the QPM service account. Keep both files outside
client-readable runtime directories.
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
qpus:
  site-qpu:
    provider: iqm
    provider-device-id: default
    url: https://provider.example/
    credential-db: qpu-users.json
  ibm-qpu:
    provider: ibm
    provider-device-id: ibm_torino
    resource-type: IBMQiskitRuntimeService
    url: https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/api/v1
    service-crn: "crn:v1:bluemix:public:quantum-computing:us-east:a/ACCT:INST::"
    credential-db: qpu-users.json
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-qpm-svc (1),
.BR qfw-services.yaml (5),
